      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The target is Kentucky's state row, not a national total or weighted average. Dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c identifies the ex parte numerator as Metric 5a1 and beneficiaries due for renewal as Metric 5. CMS's snapshot table uses this denominator. Resolution remains strictly the first published original (O) submission, rounded to one decimal."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The exact Kentucky O-row count history could not be fetched: the dataset's direct page rendered without data, and its CSV and datastore API were inaccessible through the web tool. HistoricalContext therefore contains fetched official whole-percent displays from each reporting month's initial CMS snapshot. CMS separates updated prior-month outcomes into a different section, supporting the inference that these current-period tables represent the original-report variant. Exact O numerators and tenths were not independently recovered; no counts were reconstructed from rounded percentages."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Read Kentucky's current-period Coverage Retention and Disenrollment Rates tables in https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-jan2026.pdf and https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-feb2026.pdf.",
        "result": "January 2026: 153,237 beneficiaries due for renewal, 76% renewed ex parte. February 2026: 139,700 due, 78% renewed ex parte. These are published whole-percent state shares."
